WEBVTT

00:11.150 --> 00:13.240
See you later, Moi.

00:18.330 --> 00:22.870
Thank you for always protecting me.

00:23.710 --> 00:28.290
I'm gonna train everyday
so I can become an amazing witch!

00:29.170 --> 00:33.220
So let's definitely meet again, okay?

00:42.430 --> 00:45.350
Hey, you there!

00:46.400 --> 00:49.020
Yeah, I'm talkin' to you.

00:49.320 --> 00:51.570
Morihito Otogi!

00:51.940 --> 00:54.280
Fancy meeting you here.

00:54.280 --> 00:56.820
You sure pulled off a cool stunt
the other day, didn't ya?

00:57.950 --> 00:58.870
Kelpfish?

00:58.870 --> 01:01.370
Don't you remember? It's Momota!

01:01.370 --> 01:02.290
I'm Inuzuka!

01:02.290 --> 01:03.290
I'm Saruwatari!

01:03.290 --> 01:04.250
I'm Yamamoto!

01:04.250 --> 01:05.710
<i>Shouldn't you be a pheasant?</i>

01:05.830 --> 01:09.210
Don't tell me you've already forgotten
about Graduation Day!

01:09.670 --> 01:13.090
When we were teasing Kamei,
you butted in and saved him,

01:12.840 --> 01:15.470
RYUUGUU TOWN
SHOPPING STREET

01:13.090 --> 01:15.470
and then you both escaped
to Ryuuguu Town!

01:15.760 --> 01:17.550
<i>Get your folktales in order.</i>

01:17.550 --> 01:21.390
And also, you made fun
of Momota's hairstyle, didn't you?

01:21.390 --> 01:24.560
Momota spends 30 minutes everyday
perfecting his hairstyle.

01:24.560 --> 01:26.850
It's more important to him
than his very life!

01:26.850 --> 01:28.520
<i>Momota, your life is pretty cheap.</i>

01:28.520 --> 01:30.770
Well gon-mershyuup!

01:30.770 --> 01:32.610
<i>Yamamoto, please articulate
your speech better!</i>

01:32.900 --> 01:35.690
Enough! Let's get him already!

01:35.690 --> 01:37.110
- All right!
- Awrit!

01:38.070 --> 01:38.990
What?

01:42.620 --> 01:46.120
Damn it, stay still!

01:49.790 --> 01:52.500
Why do you let them punch you, Morihito?

01:52.960 --> 01:55.760
I just purposely lose to them, Dad.

01:56.170 --> 01:59.390
If I fought back, they'd just
end up in really bad shape.

01:59.390 --> 02:02.760
You realize that line comes off
as a sore loser's cringy excuse, right?

02:02.930 --> 02:07.520
Momota's the one kid I did punch,
back when we were little. I hurt him badly.

02:07.770 --> 02:09.810
That was back then, though.

02:09.810 --> 02:13.270
You've since learned the skills
you need to control your strength.

02:13.650 --> 02:17.030
With guys like them, it's easier
to let them punch me and get it over with.

02:17.530 --> 02:20.530
Morihito, do you remember Nico?

02:23.080 --> 02:24.290
The witch Nico?

02:33.670 --> 02:35.090
When we were in fourth grade,

02:35.590 --> 02:39.220
she said she was going to the witches' Holy Land
to undergo training, and moved away.

02:39.220 --> 02:42.890
Yes. She's finished that training
and is now coming home.

02:43.220 --> 02:46.810
Plus, I'm told she wants
to make you her familiar.

02:48.680 --> 02:50.810
Spitting out your naruto fish cake
is understandable.

02:51.150 --> 02:55.400
Indeed, witches' familiars are usually animals.

02:55.400 --> 02:58.110
However, in the distant past,

02:58.110 --> 03:02.070
some familiars absorbed enough
magic to take on a human form.

03:02.620 --> 03:08.000
This happened to an ox and tiger familiar,
and they married humans and had children.

03:08.540 --> 03:11.080
And their descendants
became known as the ogres of today.

03:11.370 --> 03:15.840
In other words, our ogre clan
descends from a lineage of familiars.

03:16.090 --> 03:19.170
Yeah, I already know about our roots.

03:19.170 --> 03:22.220
It's just that in this day and age, telling
someone to become their minion is strange.

03:22.430 --> 03:24.090
People don't do that anymore.

03:24.510 --> 03:29.520
Currently, our families don't have a master-servant
relationship, but an old pact does remain.

03:29.520 --> 03:32.140
And we need to abide by the code.

03:32.190 --> 03:34.230
Then, why can’t you do it?

03:34.560 --> 03:38.820
Believe me when I tell you that I'd love to become
a manservant for a little high school witch.

03:38.820 --> 03:40.110
You'd love to?

03:40.360 --> 03:44.280
But unfortunately, I leave for a long-term
overseas business trip tomorrow.

03:44.280 --> 03:47.700
Even though you're called a familiar,
it's more like you're her bodyguard.

03:47.700 --> 03:48.910
A bodyguard?

03:48.910 --> 03:53.000
Nico's mother stayed behind
in their Holy Land for special reasons,

03:53.000 --> 03:55.580
so the only one coming home
will just be Nico.

03:55.580 --> 03:58.170
And you'll be living here by yourself, too.

03:58.590 --> 03:59.800
And so,

03:59.920 --> 04:03.760
we decided you and Nico
will live here together.

04:04.470 --> 04:06.010
Are you doing this on purpose?

04:06.260 --> 04:09.640
Ugh, what a mess.
A greasy, sloppy mess.

04:09.140 --> 04:10.640
<i>Live...</i>

04:09.640 --> 04:15.520
Oh, my poor glasses.
How could you do that to them?

04:12.310 --> 04:13.560
<i>with Nico?</i>

04:23.490 --> 04:25.820
I hope Moi's been doing well.

04:35.080 --> 04:39.380
WITCH'S RETURN

04:43.510 --> 04:44.680
I'm Morihito.

04:45.300 --> 04:46.430
Moihito.

04:47.300 --> 04:50.640
You can't pronounce it right?
Well, whatever.

04:51.180 --> 04:55.940
Mo... Moihito. Moi!

05:00.940 --> 05:04.320
I wonder how much
that klutz has grown.

05:11.950 --> 05:12.870
What the...

05:13.160 --> 05:14.660
Some kind of brave burglar?

05:15.000 --> 05:17.500
I kind of lost my balance
while I was flying,

05:17.750 --> 05:21.750
and then I kind of lost control
completely. Sorry.

05:22.000 --> 05:24.630
Wait, are you...

05:29.550 --> 05:30.760
Hi, Moi.

05:33.100 --> 05:34.100
Nico.

05:35.180 --> 05:38.060
As promised, we meet again.

05:38.690 --> 05:40.110
Well, what do you think?

05:40.110 --> 05:42.690
Do you think I've become a magnificent...

05:42.690 --> 05:44.780
Before that, let's clean the room.

05:47.320 --> 05:51.330
Man, I didn't think
it'd be within zero seconds.

05:51.490 --> 05:54.040
I thought I was prepared for it, too.

05:54.330 --> 05:58.540
I didn't think that you'd cause trouble
within zero seconds of arriving.

05:58.750 --> 06:01.420
I-I'm sorry, Moi.

06:01.420 --> 06:02.750
It's fine, don't touch anything.

06:03.630 --> 06:06.170
You're probably tired,
so sit over there and relax.

06:06.550 --> 06:07.420
Okay.

06:07.840 --> 06:09.680
Eat some cookies
that I baked this morning.

06:07.840 --> 06:09.680
WELCOME

06:10.050 --> 06:10.970
Okay.

06:13.430 --> 06:14.770
<i>So kind.</i>

06:16.100 --> 06:18.480
<i>Moi became a really handsome guy!</i>

06:18.480 --> 06:20.900
<i>Really exceeded all expectations
on how he turned out.</i>

06:20.900 --> 06:25.530
<i>He's still the same kind, blunt guy
with that one weird hair spike!</i>

06:25.530 --> 06:29.700
<i>And we'll be living together now,
so I know lots of things could happen!</i>

06:29.700 --> 06:32.490
<i>Wait, lots of things?
What kind of things?</i>

06:32.660 --> 06:35.370
<i>Even though he's an ogre, he's still a guy!</i>

06:35.370 --> 06:37.500
<i>I bet he'll look at me
like how a man looks at a woman.</i>

06:37.500 --> 06:40.620
<i>What if he's having
lewd thoughts right now?</i>

06:40.620 --> 06:41.420
Nico.

06:41.420 --> 06:42.590
Oh, yes?

06:42.750 --> 06:46.800
I know this is happening all so suddenly,
and it's leaving me a little perplexed.

06:47.260 --> 06:48.800
But I hope we can work things out.

06:50.470 --> 06:54.640
Yeah, me too.
And I'm sorry about all this.

06:54.760 --> 06:57.060
Things like being
my bodyguard and roommate...

06:57.060 --> 06:59.520
My mom just decided it all on her own.

06:59.520 --> 07:02.610
Well, if there's a contract,
we just have to accept it, right?

07:03.730 --> 07:05.270
I'm gonna take care of this glass.

07:05.270 --> 07:06.610
Oh, right.

07:06.940 --> 07:09.650
I can fix the broken window
with my magic!

07:09.900 --> 07:10.820
Really?

07:12.070 --> 07:14.240
Did you forget who I was?

07:14.410 --> 07:15.870
The person who broke the glass.

07:15.870 --> 07:19.000
In order to use this spell,
I'll need a medium.

07:19.160 --> 07:20.580
A medium?

07:20.580 --> 07:23.500
Moi, do you have an item
that is precious to you?

07:24.080 --> 07:25.250
I don't really understand, but...

07:25.790 --> 07:30.050
How about my favorite vintage mug?
It's really important to me.

07:30.050 --> 07:31.260
That's perfect.

07:33.840 --> 07:35.510
Okay, here we go.

07:43.400 --> 07:46.190
Witch Recovery!

07:50.610 --> 07:51.950
It really got fixed!

07:52.110 --> 07:53.200
Amazing!

07:53.200 --> 07:55.030
Way too easy!

07:56.030 --> 07:57.080
What was that sound?

07:57.370 --> 08:00.580
It's the sound of your sacrificed mug
being broken to smithereens.

08:00.580 --> 08:03.120
Wait, what?! Sacrificed?

08:03.120 --> 08:04.080
You see,

08:04.290 --> 08:08.380
this spell works off of the feelings of
care and value that people have for items.

08:08.380 --> 08:10.460
Say that first! Don't say it so proudly!

08:10.670 --> 08:12.970
What the hell? I really liked this mug!

08:12.970 --> 08:15.680
And it's those feelings
that made it possible to fix the window.

08:15.680 --> 08:17.470
But you broke it!

08:18.220 --> 08:22.480
Y-You're right, I guess we should've
used one of my things, huh?

08:23.060 --> 08:24.650
I'm sorry, Moi.

08:25.560 --> 08:27.270
I guess I'm no good.

08:27.270 --> 08:32.190
I still end up relying on you
for everything, just like I did as a kid.

08:32.190 --> 08:33.950
No, you have changed.

08:35.360 --> 08:39.580
The window is fixed, after all.
Magic is amazing, huh?

08:42.040 --> 08:44.290
I almost didn't recognize you, Nico.

08:46.580 --> 08:48.460
Really?

08:48.460 --> 08:50.880
In that case, I'll show you
some of my other spells!

08:50.880 --> 08:52.630
No, you really don't...

08:52.630 --> 08:54.260
Which one should I show you?

08:54.470 --> 08:58.010
I know! Maybe magic
that makes things as flat as paper.

08:58.010 --> 08:58.890
What now?

08:59.010 --> 09:01.470
Is there something
that I can make as flat as paper?

09:01.470 --> 09:02.270
No!

09:02.520 --> 09:04.310
Don't worry, it'll go back to the way it was.

09:04.310 --> 09:06.520
You're saying that
after my mug got smashed to pieces!

09:06.980 --> 09:09.820
But I want to show you my magic.

09:10.190 --> 09:12.570
That's right. I'll just cast it on myself.

09:13.780 --> 09:15.280
Flip Flap Flat!

09:19.280 --> 09:20.280
Nico!

09:20.450 --> 09:21.950
Are you okay, Nico?

09:21.950 --> 09:24.290
Moi, I umm...

09:24.620 --> 09:27.540
My vision's swaying
all over the place for some reason.

09:27.670 --> 09:30.000
What do I look like right now?

09:30.000 --> 09:31.500
You've become as flat as paper!

09:31.500 --> 09:32.590
Oh, no.

09:33.210 --> 09:35.010
I feel really nauseous.

09:35.380 --> 09:38.090
My innards are doing the wave.

09:38.550 --> 09:40.800
I-I have to get back to how I was.

09:42.260 --> 09:44.600
You're kidding me! Nico!

09:46.060 --> 09:47.940
She went over that like a high jumper!

09:47.940 --> 09:50.980
Her carelessness hasn't changed at all.

09:51.730 --> 09:53.320
Nico!

09:54.280 --> 09:57.070
I feel sick. I'm gonna barf.

09:58.660 --> 10:00.370
Her barf is like confetti!

10:00.740 --> 10:01.620
Wait!

10:02.910 --> 10:05.410
Damn it, how far is she going to go?

10:14.460 --> 10:16.470
- She fell in the crack?
- I fell in the crack?

10:17.590 --> 10:18.470
Damn it!

10:18.720 --> 10:22.220
Nico! Do you have some kind of spell
you could use to get out of there?

10:22.220 --> 10:23.850
N-Not really.

10:23.970 --> 10:26.430
Oh, let me get a vacuum cleaner
from the house.

10:26.430 --> 10:28.390
Moi, this might be bad.

10:29.020 --> 10:32.520
I think the spell
is going to wear off soon.

10:32.610 --> 10:34.610
If I go back to normal right here,

10:34.940 --> 10:37.490
I'll really become flat.

10:37.610 --> 10:40.160
Wh-What should I do?

10:40.160 --> 10:41.240
Hey!

10:41.370 --> 10:43.660
What the hell're you doing
in front of my house?

10:44.030 --> 10:45.370
- Kelpfish!
- It's Momota!

10:45.540 --> 10:46.750
Wait, this is your house?

10:46.750 --> 10:50.460
That's right! You knew that and wanted
to get revenge on me, didn't you?

10:50.460 --> 10:51.380
No!

10:51.830 --> 10:54.750
Oh, right. A vacuum cleaner!
Let me borrow your vacuum cleaner!

10:54.750 --> 10:57.090
There's something stuck
in this crack and I can't get it out.

10:58.090 --> 10:59.760
Is that the kind of attitude you have
when you ask—

10:59.760 --> 11:02.390
I'll grovel if you want me to.
Just please hurry!

11:03.050 --> 11:04.390
Why're you getting all serious?

11:04.390 --> 11:05.890
There's no time!

11:07.060 --> 11:08.520
What, you wanna fight?

11:08.680 --> 11:11.730
Oh wait, you can't though, huh?!

11:13.730 --> 11:14.900
Geez.

11:15.110 --> 11:18.530
Doesn't your son know anything
about holding back?

11:19.740 --> 11:22.030
Come on, stop it!

11:22.030 --> 11:23.320
Take that!

11:23.950 --> 11:25.330
Moi!

11:26.290 --> 11:29.290
You just wanted to look cool
in front of a girl!

11:29.660 --> 11:32.790
And now you can't punch me anymore!

11:32.920 --> 11:36.800
- Take that! And that!
- Moi! Oh no, Moi!

11:39.170 --> 11:42.680
You did well to hold back.
I'm proud of you.

11:42.890 --> 11:45.350
Why do we even have ogre powers?

11:45.600 --> 11:48.310
All it does is cause pointless fights.

11:48.560 --> 11:51.560
I end up hurting them,
or can't even protect anyone.

11:52.020 --> 11:53.600
It's all just terrible.

11:54.400 --> 11:58.360
Morihito, if you wish to,
you can begin training.

11:58.690 --> 11:59.740
Training?

11:59.740 --> 12:02.950
"Ogre Qigong." It's been passed down
through the ogre family line.

12:03.240 --> 12:06.370
If you learn it, you'll be able
to utilize your strength better.

12:07.280 --> 12:13.040
Besides, even if you don't use it,
merely "having" strength is important.

12:13.330 --> 12:15.830
It will make your heart strong.

12:16.500 --> 12:17.880
What do you think, Morihito?

12:18.250 --> 12:19.760
Are you ready for this?

12:27.300 --> 12:28.060
Yeah.

12:30.640 --> 12:33.190
So let's definitely meet again, okay?

12:33.600 --> 12:36.940
I'll learn magic that fixes wounds.

12:38.190 --> 12:39.440
<i>That's right.</i>

12:39.530 --> 12:41.240
We can just fix it.

12:42.110 --> 12:43.780
There's nothing to be afraid of.

12:44.610 --> 12:46.320
We have magic.

12:47.530 --> 12:49.620
So I can just blast it.

12:52.790 --> 12:57.000
All right, I get it! A vacuum cleaner?
I'll get it right now!

12:57.250 --> 12:59.040
<i>Ogre Qigong Fighting Style...</i>

13:00.300 --> 13:01.760
<i>Metal Club!</i>

13:00.300 --> 13:01.760
METAL CLUB

13:07.390 --> 13:09.470
This was perfect for breaking the wall.

13:12.770 --> 13:13.390
Nico!

13:21.440 --> 13:23.150
Moi!

13:23.150 --> 13:24.360
I made it.

13:24.610 --> 13:26.410
What?

13:26.410 --> 13:30.780
Wait, are you Nico
from when we were kids?

13:30.990 --> 13:34.250
Oh, are you that bully, um, Kelpfish?

13:34.250 --> 13:35.410
Quit calling me that!

13:35.410 --> 13:39.630
Wait a minute, what're you gonna do
about my wall here? It's practically destroyed!

13:39.630 --> 13:40.920
Yeah, I know.

13:41.170 --> 13:43.550
Nico, can you use your Witch Recovery?

13:43.550 --> 13:47.050
I can, but we'd need something
that's really important to someone.

13:47.050 --> 13:48.180
I've got you covered.

13:48.890 --> 13:51.810
He's got something here
that's more important than his life.

13:56.440 --> 14:00.190
Now hold on a second here,
the wall got fixed but now I'm bald!

14:00.480 --> 14:02.690
Thanks for letting us use your hair.

14:02.690 --> 14:08.200
Can you please tell me what happened?
What the hell are you guys?

14:08.320 --> 14:10.820
That turned into a really big ordeal.

14:10.820 --> 14:12.910
Sorry Moi.

14:13.200 --> 14:16.620
By the way, we had Kelpfish pay the price,
but was that okay?

14:16.620 --> 14:17.710
It's fine.

14:18.170 --> 14:19.630
We're even now.

14:22.250 --> 14:24.960
Well everything turned out fine,
so let's go home.

14:24.960 --> 14:27.010
Oh, um, Moi?

14:29.800 --> 14:31.970
I have a favor to ask.

14:36.430 --> 14:40.690
I know you're starting a new life and all,
but isn't this a little too much?

14:40.690 --> 14:41.860
My arms are gonna break off.

14:41.860 --> 14:43.480
Oh come on now.

14:43.610 --> 14:46.650
You're an ogre, so something
like this should be easy-peasy.

14:46.740 --> 14:47.650
I know!

14:47.650 --> 14:52.030
For my very fragile familiar, I shall cast
a spell to make things easy for you.

14:53.990 --> 14:55.950
Super Light!

14:58.750 --> 15:00.420
Okay, now try to pick it up.

15:02.380 --> 15:03.130
So light!

15:03.380 --> 15:06.880
Whoa, it's so light that it made me
instinctively say, "So light!"

15:06.880 --> 15:10.760
It's a spell that makes things light!
But what's with that face?

15:10.840 --> 15:12.010
You try holding it.

15:12.010 --> 15:12.890
What?

15:13.930 --> 15:14.760
So light!

15:16.020 --> 15:18.520
Nico, your magic is pretty useful.

15:21.270 --> 15:22.770
That's right!

15:22.770 --> 15:25.820
My magic is pretty useful!

15:25.820 --> 15:29.030
It's almost as useful as a zip lock bag.

15:31.240 --> 15:35.580
Nico, do you really plan to let
the whole city know that you're a witch?

15:36.790 --> 15:39.000
If people found out
that you can use magic,

15:39.000 --> 15:40.580
that would attract all kinds of people.

15:41.290 --> 15:44.040
And that might put you in a bad situation.

15:46.000 --> 15:48.130
So do you want me
to stay locked inside the house?

15:48.130 --> 15:50.090
That would definitely avoid risks.

15:50.090 --> 15:51.840
I understand what you're saying.

15:52.130 --> 15:56.850
However, there's an ironclad rule that witches
are supposed to use their magic to help people.

15:57.180 --> 16:00.600
Novice witches' magic is still unstable.

16:00.600 --> 16:04.190
The best way to stabilize it
is to interact with people, build relationships,

16:04.190 --> 16:05.980
and help those around them.

16:06.320 --> 16:10.110
On the opposite side of that, if you're alone,
you'll get lured to dark magic.

16:10.440 --> 16:14.320
So you're saying its best to interact
with people while using your magic?

16:14.320 --> 16:17.540
Yes, and I know
this will be a burden for you,

16:17.540 --> 16:21.250
but right now is an important time period
for me to complete my training.

16:21.750 --> 16:26.000
Because I want to become
a wonderful witch who can help people!

16:29.590 --> 16:31.760
<i>So Nico has a dream, huh?</i>

16:32.380 --> 16:34.340
All right, I get it.

16:35.300 --> 16:36.600
I'm a familiar.

16:37.100 --> 16:41.180
So if you want to become a grand witch,
then I'll help you achieve that.

16:43.940 --> 16:45.440
WITCH GIRL IN LOVE
NICO

16:45.440 --> 16:47.690
WILL WE START DATING MOI?

16:47.230 --> 16:49.780
Geez, it's like he's a little too serious.

16:49.780 --> 16:52.150
If we ever dated,
I think things will get too heavy.

16:52.150 --> 16:54.780
Like he'll send me super long text messages.

16:54.780 --> 16:58.530
But you know what?
That's the part that makes me wonder.

16:58.660 --> 17:00.200
And it kind of sets me on fire?

17:00.200 --> 17:01.120
It's on fire!

17:01.120 --> 17:02.830
- Yep!
- No really, it's on fire!

17:02.830 --> 17:03.580
What?

17:03.750 --> 17:04.960
- It's a fire!
- What?

17:05.170 --> 17:06.830
- There's someone there!
- Please help me!

17:07.040 --> 17:08.420
She couldn't get out in time.

17:09.710 --> 17:11.010
I'm gonna go help her!

17:11.130 --> 17:12.510
No, it's too dangerous!

17:12.510 --> 17:15.010
Can you even save someone
while flying in the air?

17:15.260 --> 17:17.390
Plus there're way too many people.

17:17.390 --> 17:18.600
But I said earlier...

17:19.100 --> 17:22.430
Magic is for helping people.

17:27.810 --> 17:28.730
All right.

17:30.270 --> 17:33.320
You concentrate on flying,
and I'll rescue the person!

17:33.320 --> 17:34.150
Okay!

17:34.490 --> 17:36.570
Help me! Please help!

17:37.280 --> 17:38.780
Are you all right?

17:39.620 --> 17:40.660
What's that?

17:40.660 --> 17:41.870
Something's flying!

17:42.410 --> 17:45.040
- Is there anyone else in there?
- N-No, it's just me.

17:45.040 --> 17:46.620
Okay, jump on over here then.

17:46.620 --> 17:47.420
What?

17:47.580 --> 17:49.000
O-Okay!

17:53.590 --> 17:54.510
Nico!

17:54.510 --> 17:56.010
We're over the weight limit!

17:56.010 --> 17:58.720
Looks like my wand
can't carry three people!

17:59.600 --> 18:00.930
We're gonna hit the ground!

18:01.100 --> 18:04.060
Nico! Cast the magic
that makes you light onto me!

18:04.390 --> 18:07.350
Got it! Super Light!

18:10.520 --> 18:13.030
We did it!
Moi, we became really light!

18:13.110 --> 18:15.780
That's totally awesome!

18:15.780 --> 18:18.740
Just trust me and everything
will be honky-dorey!

18:18.740 --> 18:19.490
So light-hearted!

18:19.490 --> 18:22.580
Hey pretty lady, you can thank me
by giving me your digits, maybe?

18:22.580 --> 18:24.660
Moi's getting all flirty now.

18:24.660 --> 18:28.170
Or maybe we can even go for some dinner?
You know, some din-din?

18:25.250 --> 18:29.580
Oh, so if you cast Super Light on someone,
their personality becomes light-hearted.

18:28.170 --> 18:31.880
Sound good? Or how bout we go to a party?
A party, yay yay!

18:29.580 --> 18:32.210
Um, what's going on by the way?

18:31.880 --> 18:35.590
We'll have, like, literally the best time ever.
You don't wanna miss out!

18:32.210 --> 18:35.340
We're flying together like it's nothing.
Who are you two?

18:35.340 --> 18:37.260
Oh, um...

18:37.260 --> 18:40.090
Check it out, this girl's totally a witch!
Magic and everything. Awesome, right?

18:40.090 --> 18:40.970
So light!

18:40.970 --> 18:43.810
Did you really just say that?
After you told me not to!

18:43.810 --> 18:44.600
A witch?

18:44.600 --> 18:46.680
Yep, that's right! And I'm totally an ogre!

18:46.680 --> 18:47.390
An ogre?

18:47.390 --> 18:48.940
You keep blabbing!

18:49.690 --> 18:53.320
Woopsie, looks like three people
is still too much.

18:53.320 --> 18:57.950
Hey yo, Nico! Before we all hit the ground
screaming with this beauty,

18:58.450 --> 19:01.120
let's park our butts
over at the park, you get me?

19:01.120 --> 19:05.870
Moi, please, don't talk right now.
It's really dangerous!

19:06.370 --> 19:08.000
Oh, geez!

19:08.660 --> 19:10.330
Woo! Ace landing, yeah!

19:09.370 --> 19:11.080
NICO CAST SUPER LIGHT ON HERSELF!

19:10.330 --> 19:11.080
Light-hearted!

19:12.210 --> 19:13.630
Oh, um...

19:14.420 --> 19:18.220
Thank you very much
for saving my life.

19:18.340 --> 19:20.180
Yeah! Yay! Woo!

19:20.180 --> 19:21.340
Yeah!

19:21.340 --> 19:22.220
They're so cheerful.

19:22.680 --> 19:25.350
So, what on earth are you two...

19:25.350 --> 19:26.470
Aw fudgsicles, Moi!

19:26.640 --> 19:28.730
We left all our stuff
that we bought back there!

19:32.520 --> 19:33.560
Wait, what?

19:33.940 --> 19:36.610
We gotta nab our stuff
before we skidaddle home!

19:36.610 --> 19:40.990
See you later, Miss! Thanks for sharing
a magical time with us!

19:41.860 --> 19:44.660
So very light-hearted.

19:45.830 --> 19:46.950
So very heavy!

19:47.910 --> 19:49.870
My arms are gonna break off.

19:49.870 --> 19:52.960
Why did our stuff become so heavy?

19:54.130 --> 19:58.090
The spell's effect wore off,
so as a drawback, it got heavy.

19:58.090 --> 20:00.380
A drawback? That kind of thing happens?

20:01.760 --> 20:03.840
M-My body feels really heavy.

20:04.220 --> 20:06.970
I-It's heavy like lead.

20:07.260 --> 20:09.270
Another drawback?

20:10.230 --> 20:12.100
M-Me, too.

20:15.900 --> 20:17.360
Okay, so...

20:17.610 --> 20:19.740
The window gets broken,
you became flat as paper,

20:19.740 --> 20:22.150
went flying off with a whoosh,
and then slipped into a crack.

20:22.150 --> 20:24.160
After that, we rescued someone
from a fire.

20:24.160 --> 20:26.120
If that was the kind of day
I was going to have,

20:26.120 --> 20:28.160
I wish someone
would tell me ahead of time.

20:28.580 --> 20:31.960
We should communicate more.
When I message you, respond right away.

20:29.870 --> 20:31.960
It's hard, being doubted like that.

20:31.960 --> 20:34.380
It's not like I'm trying
to make things difficult for you.

20:31.960 --> 20:34.830
There's really no reason why you can't.

20:34.380 --> 20:38.630
No one understands me.
There is no safe place for me here.

20:34.830 --> 20:38.630
I mean, it's a given that as your bodyguard,
I should always know what you're doing.

20:39.460 --> 20:41.090
That's pretty heavy, Nico.

20:41.380 --> 20:42.760
You too, Moi.

20:45.090 --> 20:46.890
We'll be starting our new lives tomorrow,

20:47.350 --> 20:51.140
so I may be inexperienced, but I hope
you can take care of me for a long time.

20:51.310 --> 20:53.640
Don't say a weird thing like that
while sitting on a futon.

20:53.640 --> 20:55.770
And go sleep in your own room!

20:56.610 --> 20:58.070
Okay.

21:00.940 --> 21:03.450
Hey, Moi.

21:04.410 --> 21:07.280
Thank you for everything today.

21:08.120 --> 21:11.540
It's amazing that you can control
your ogre strength like that.

21:12.040 --> 21:13.910
You must've trained really hard.

21:15.170 --> 21:17.040
Yeah, I did.

21:20.710 --> 21:25.680
There's a prophecy that within a year,
disaster will befall Nico.

21:26.840 --> 21:30.600
Since her mother is an oracle,
she divined the near future,

21:30.600 --> 21:32.890
and that was the result that came up.

21:32.890 --> 21:36.190
We don't know the details yet. But...

21:36.440 --> 21:41.190
when she tried to divine a way to stave
that disaster off, this was the answer.

21:41.860 --> 21:44.240
"The protector shall be a familiar."

21:46.780 --> 21:48.950
<i>My mission is to protect Nico.</i>

21:49.530 --> 21:53.450
<i>We should hide the fact that she's a witch,
and try not to stand out as much.</i>

21:54.040 --> 21:55.460
<i>And for that to happen...</i>

21:57.170 --> 21:58.710
<i>Moi.</i>

21:59.960 --> 22:01.050
<i>I love you.</i>

22:04.340 --> 22:06.720
To handle the trouble
that she herself causes...

22:07.130 --> 22:08.970
I'll have to add that to my mission, too.

22:08.970 --> 22:09.850
Huh?

22:09.970 --> 22:11.100
What is it?

22:11.100 --> 22:12.470
Oh, nothing.

22:12.640 --> 22:15.180
What? Just tell me.

22:15.180 --> 22:19.060
<i>Thus begins the unusual living situation
between a witch and an ogre.</i>

22:15.180 --> 22:20.360
Oh come on, don't just sit there
and brood, tell me.

22:19.440 --> 22:25.740
<i>The words, "grim prospects" stab
at the ogre like a horn to his head.</i>

22:20.360 --> 22:24.860
If you don't tell me,
I'll cast a spell so you can't fall asleep.

23:57.790 --> 23:59.000
Good morning sunshine!

23:59.000 --> 24:02.670
How was the first episode? Uh huh,
I know right? It was super fun!

24:02.670 --> 24:04.130
You're too excited!

24:04.130 --> 24:07.000
There's an ominous prophecy involved,
you know. But I'll keep that a secret.

24:07.000 --> 24:08.420
Oh, this is the next episode preview!

24:07.550 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
A GIANT ROOKIE
LET'S GO TO A DINER
THE FLYING CLASSROOM

24:08.420 --> 24:10.720
Okay, next episode!
Our cover gets blown at school!

24:10.720 --> 24:11.970
She just said all of it!
